Whether a public chain can run an ecosystem does not hinge on marketing, but on whether developers are willing to stay long-term.
@Vanar  chooses to define the functions of public chains in reverse, starting from games and entertainment content. This shows that it is not purely concerned with TPS numbers, but whether the game runs smoothly on the chain, whether asset interactions are low-cost enough, and whether players are deterred by complex on-chain processes. For players, blockchain should not be a burden, but rather an infrastructure that exists without feeling.

#vanar  tries to leave the complexity of blockchain at the bottom layer, while leaving a simple and direct development experience for the team.

